  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sales from sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "No problem—the correction from “flower stall” to “flower shop” does not change the calculation.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold an average of\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks. Since the number of individual sunflowers in each bouquet isn’t specified, we can’t calculate the total sunflower revenue yet. We would need the number of sunflowers per bouquet.\n\nIf each bouquet contains \\(n\\) sunflowers, then the 12 bouquets generated:\n\n\\[\n12n \\times \\$3 = \\$36n\n\\]\n\nin sunflower sales.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday earns \\$26 per day from individual sunflowers. Over 3 days:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times \\$26 = \\$78\n\\]\n\nEach individual sunflower sells for \\$3, so:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$78}{\\$3}=26\n\\]\n\nThus, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nThe bouquet information means he sold \\(3\\times(56\\div 8)=21\\) bouquets, but the number of sunflowers in those bouquets is not specified.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\times \\$26}{\\$3}=26\n\\]\n\n- Bouquets sold:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\times \\$56}{\\$8}=21\n\\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:\n\n\\[\n21 \\times 12=252\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers priced at \\$2 each:\n\n**Individual sunflowers over 3 days:**\n\n\\[\n3 \\times \\$26 = \\$78\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\$78 \\div \\$2 = 39\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold 39 individual sunflowers.\n\n**Sunflowers in bouquets:**\n\n\\[\n3 \\times \\left(\\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}\\right)=21\\text{ bouquets}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n21 \\times 12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n\\]\n\n**Total sunflowers:**\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
